Hmm, AFAIK Miatas don't have a halt button... There might be a jumber on 
the motherboard that turns the reset button into a halt button. (At least 
the alphastation 500 such a jumper.)

> which console ?

SRM maybe? Except it's an A and not an AU, so I don't know...

> Someone told me that it can be a problem with the video card, the actual 
> video card is on ISA slot (it seems to me). And i can't find a list of 
> compatible video card.

It should be a PCI card. Many shipped with Powerstorm cards (which are 
actually made by Intergraph, and only have binary drivers for Tru64 and 
Windoze. I've had good luck with Matrox cards. Sometimes they are finicky 
about what slot you put them in though.

If you're getting video output, that probably isn't the problem though.

> do you know where i can find some info ?

It might be helpful if you could post the exact output. You can connect a 
serial line to serial port 1, and unplug the keyboard to get output there.

Ivan

PS: If it's not too much trouble, could you tell me the positions of all 
the jumpers and dip switches on your motherboard. (Just the upper part 
with the CPU, not the part with the ISA and PCI slots.) I have a 433au 
with a 500 MHz chip that I'd like to actually be able to run at 500 MHz. 
I haven't been able to find any documentation on this :(



