>500au (MIATA) running DigitalUnix 4.0E due to addition of
>some external devices. Does anyone know a way to do this
>without a complete installation from scratch?

Coming from VMS-land I know very little about Digital Unix.

Is the problem that the device names for your existing disks might change?  

If so, here's how I'd handle it.

1.  >>>SET AUTO_ACTION HALT
2.  Power down the system and add the card.
3.  Power up the system and use >>>SHOW DEV to see the new devices.  If they
haven't changed, you're probably home free.
4.  If they have changed, power down the computer and remove the board. 
Then boot it and edit /etc/fstab to reflect the new configuration.
5.  Power down, re-install the card, power up, set the new BOOTDEF_DEV, and
go.

There's a hole in this in that if you screw up step 4 you end up with an
unuseable system, maybe somebody more unix-savvy can give a better
suggestion.

