In article <1110544125.491176.291200@l41g2000cwc.googlegroups.com>, hinnersd@nycap.rr.com writes:
:Anyone know where I can find a FSL for this architecture?

  The failsafe loader is the piece that tries to load the firmware.
  (If the failsafe loader -- this box apparently called it the
  failsafe boot, FWIW -- is active, then you need the firmware on
  CD or floppy, and not the loader itself.)

:...I tried making one from dec2000_v2_2.sys with mkboot.exe
:but that didn't seem to do anything.

  What you apparently need here are the bits, and how to generate
  the disks is covered at the Alpha SRM firmware website.

    http://h18002.www1.hp.com/alphaserver/archive/axp/dec2000.html
    http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/archive/dec2000.html

  The failsafe loader (failsafe boot) is looking for jnupdate.exe,
  according to the documentation.  (This filename may well have been
  changed to fwupdate to match other boxes, I do not know.)  Again,
  according to the documentation, the box does appear to display what
  it is looking for.  (It's been quite some time since I've worked
  with a DEC 2000 series box, FWIW.)

  The OpenVMS FAQ has some pointers to related materials, as well.


